 it over and we're  going to take the edge here and fold it  across to the opposite edge so just take  it round it off a little bit in the  middle meet up the two edges here so you  need to just round it right here like  that meet the two edges together hold  them and then take your finger and just  pull in here a little bit to round that  off as best you can because it will be  very thick and then you can kind of  flatten it out like that holding these  two edges together then you can crease  it all the  lay down so if you like to set it down  on the table and just give it a crease  and that is it that's how you make the  paper popper now to load it all we need  to do is to grab it by this edge right  here so you'll see we have this little  bar or section we're going to pinch it  right here at this point where it meets  the rest of the paper and what we're  going to do is to just lift it up so if  you want to you could stick your finger  underneath it and lift it like that and  then pinch it and we're going to take  this edge of the paper and bring it down  and when you do that you'll see that  this corner here and this corner here go  below this edge so you're gonna pull it  down until those corners go directly  below this edge like this once they do  you're going to grab these two edges  together and pinch them so just take the  two edges and grab those corners and  pinch them together like that and that's  it you want to make sure that you're not  pinching this edge in between these  corners too tightly otherwise this part  cannot lift up which is what allows the  paper popper to pop by catching air in  this pocket so let's go ahead and give  it a try so you want to grab these two  corners on the bottom and this edge  right here this sliding edge should be  right around this corner or above right  there and then you're just going to  basically throw it like you're throwing  a ball just like that and as you'll see  the pocket open back up so when you do  reload it you need to open it fold it  back down one time and then you could  reload it once again just make sure  you're not grabbing this edge or  pinching it because if you're pinching  it in between here it will not ever pop  because it won't catch the air and it  won't lift up so just make sure it's  right there or above and then do it  there you go you can also change your  paper popper into a really cool stunt  glider that can do flips and come back  to you with some folds experimenting at  practice it's pretty simple and it looks  just like this and just know if you use  the paper popper a lot it's going to  probably start to rip a little bit and  if it does it probably won't make the  best plane because it's not going to be  aerodynamic like that so you might as  well just keep it as a paper  and just start making a new one from  scratch if you want to try to make the  plane it's going to fold these edges of  the popper down and then fold the  outside up just like that hold the  bottom here about an inch from the  bottom and just take one of these edges  here and bring it down on your thumb and  line up this edge with the bottom edge  here like that about an inch from the  bottom right there should be fine and  then crease it all the way across just  like that and then do the same on the  other side by just taking the edge  meeting it up and rounding it off a  little bit with this one and then you  can crease it and then do that all the  way across the top again so you should  have something that looks just like this  then only you need to do is to fold the  outside up about a centimeter or so so  if you want to use your pinky as a guide  just about that width maybe like right  there again it's pretty forgiving it's  not you know it's not going to matter  whether you fold it off a little bit or  if it's if it's shorter or longer just  experiment with it and give it a shot  and you could just try out different  types and see which one flies they're  all gonna fly different you're gonna  find that they're all going to probably  fly a little bit different some might  come back some might do flips but there  you go let's give it a shot and see how  it flies okay so here's the plane I just  finished from the popper and there's a  couple ways you can try to throw it you  can throw it straight out you can tilt  it up like this and toss it almost  straight up or you could hold it  sideways and also toss it upside down  and up so just try experiment with a  whole bunch of different ways of  throwing it and you'll see that it'll  actually it'll change depending on how  you throw it so I'm gonna try to throw  it like this tilting it to the left and  see what happens  so there you go pretty much kind of came  back to me a little bit there just like  that  [Music]  thanks for watching my tutorial for the  paper popper stunts glider I hope you  guys enjoyed it and if you did be sure  to give it a thumbs up or like down  below and don't forget to click that  subscribe and notification bell if  you're not already leave me a comment  down below let me know were you able to  do it did you have any trouble did you  like it better than the old one I think  it's a lot better because the pocket on  the old one is so much smaller I  understand why people were having some  difficulty getting it to pop whereas  this one the pockets a lot bigger and  you can actually open this a little more  and kind of pop it easier in my opinion  be sure to practice it and that you're  not holding the edge down just like I  said also practice your throws with the  glider and try different things  different angles different curves and  maybe just try different folds in it as  well me and Jeremy Shafer are working on  a new transforming ninja star that looks  just like this and transforms like that  let me know if you want to see it leave  a comment down below and also I'll put a  poll up in the corner here let me know  if you guys want to see that next I hope  you guys enjoyed your Thanksgiving in  holidays and I'll be sure to see you  soon til next time

